{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the probabilities of the lotteries and considers differences in probabilities as negligible. It then compares the maximum outcomes of the two lotteries. Lottery A has a maximum outcome of 6000 Euros with a 45% probability, while Lottery B has a maximum outcome of 3000 Euros with a 90% probability. The probability difference between the two lotteries for the maximum outcome is 45 percentage points (90% vs. 45%), which the reason treats as negligible. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A because it offers the more favorable (higher) maximum outcome (6000 > 3000).",
